NAME
    callers - find static call and jump references to an address

SYNOPSIS
    callers <addr> [<scanstart> <scanlen>]

DESCRIPTION
    Scans CpuBus for instructions that statically call or jump to hex
    address <addr>. By default the scan covers <addr>'s own bank from
    $8000 to $FFFF; supply hex <scanstart> and <scanlen> to scan a
    different range.

    Because the scan is static, it finds every direct call or jump site in
    code regardless of whether that path executed during the current
    session. Indirect jumps and computed jump tables are not visible to
    static analysis; use bt(1) or bp(1) for runtime transfers.

EXAMPLES
    callers 8000
    callers 808000 808000 8000

EXIT STATUS
    0   Scan completed (or usage message printed).
    1   No target attached, invalid hex argument, or session service fault.

SEE ALSO
    writers(1), readers(1), disasm(1), bt(1), bp(1)
